{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9a1e1886-85c7-4026-8574-0364975d813e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the Soft 404 issue and the fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-Vxs5qc/ANSWER.md), and [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-Vxs5qc/site/robots.txt) has been updated.\n\n### Summary of Cause and Fix\n\n- **Cause:** The site is a client-side JavaScript application ([app.js](file:///tmp/h-Vxs5qc/site/app.js)) that dynamically fetches content from `/v1/notes/${slug}`. When `Disallow: /v1/` was added to `robots.txt` on 2026-09-07, Googlebot was prevented from fetching the note data when rendering pages. The client-side fetch failed into its `catch` block and rendered the `\"NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address\"` fallback screen with an HTTP 200 response, which Google classified as a Soft 404.\n- **Fix:** Updated [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-Vxs5qc/site/robots.txt) with Google's longest-match precedence:\n  ```robots.txt\n  User-agent: *\n  Allow: /v1/notes\n  Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\n  Disallow: /v1/\n  Disallow: /admin/\n\n  Sitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\n  ```\n  `Allow: /v1/notes` wins on note pages and listings, allowing Googlebot to render the content, while keeping private and per-user endpoints (`/v1/notes/*/reactions`, `/v1/me`, `/v1/auth/token`) disallowed.\n","duration_seconds":98.999102,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":107837,"output_tokens":2420,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":87960,"total_tokens":110257}}}
